ORIGIN OF THIS IMPLEMENTATION
=============================

This is an independent, clean-room implementation of read support for the VHD
and VHDX virtual disk formats, written in Go against the publicly published
format specifications listed below.

It contains no code derived from, translated from, or copied out of any other
VHD/VHDX implementation. In particular it shares no code with libvhdi or libewf,
the C libraries of similar name and purpose. Releases before 0.2.0 declared
`Author = "libewf contributors"`; that string was incorrect and has been
corrected. No code from those projects was ever incorporated.


SPECIFICATIONS USED
===================

VHD
    "Virtual Hard Disk Image Format Specification", version 1.0, Microsoft
    Corporation. Published under the Microsoft Open Specification Promise.

    Structures implemented: file footer, dynamic disk header, block allocation
    table, block sector bitmaps, parent locator entries.

    Note on checksums: this specification defines the footer and dynamic disk
    header checksum as "a one's complement of the sum of all the bytes ...
    without the checksum field". It is not a CRC. Applying a CRC to these
    structures rejects every conformant VHD image.

VHDX
    "[MS-VHDX]: Virtual Hard Disk v2 (VHDX) File Format", Microsoft Corporation.
    Published under the Microsoft Open Specification Promise.

    Structures implemented: file identifier, image headers, region table,
    metadata table and items, block allocation table with interleaved sector
    bitmap entries, sector bitmap blocks, and the log with its entry headers,
    data and zero descriptors, and data sectors.

    Note on checksums: VHDX uses CRC-32C (Castagnoli, polynomial 0x82F63B78) for
    its headers, region tables and log entries. This differs from the VHD
    checksum above; the two must not be interchanged.


CROSS-VALIDATION
================

Correctness is checked against implementations developed independently of this
one. `scripts/gen-corpus.ps1` produces authentic images using Microsoft's
Hyper-V `New-VHD` cmdlet and raw reference dumps using qemu-img, then the corpus
tests compare this library's decoded output against those dumps byte for byte.
Neither tool's source is used or redistributed here; they serve only as external
oracles during testing.


THIRD-PARTY CODE
================

None. This module has no dependencies beyond the Go standard library. See go.mod.
